 "method": {
  "topology": "SDK client, HPIC and HPIS as three processes on one host; two loopback TLS 1.3 hops (HPIC->HPIS mutual TLS); all tenants in one HPIS process / one SQLite file; one shared persistent client connection; concurrency 1",
  "timing": "SDK entry with the raw query -> SDK returns decoded plaintext records; result checks and FP64 reference outside the timer",
  "design": "per round: scenario blocks in random order; per block: warm-up, then every query once in random order, grouped into runs of 1 query; within a run each arm issues the run's queries back to back and every arm order (AB/BA, or all 6 for three arms) occurs once per consecutive group of runs; no two arms share a tenant; client cyclic GC frozen between blocks and paused within a block (servers unchanged)",
  "vector_kernel": "FP32 GEMV (data @ q, single-thread BLAS) + np.partition top-K + (score, id) stable tie-break via hpis.codec.nearest; PPE adds RAP norm projection",
  "ppe_rerank": "HPIS: production PPE fast search for Top-40 (bodies stay AES-GCM); HPIC: decrypts them with the DEK it already holds, re-ranks with the same FP32 kernel on the normalized vector stored inside each body (holder-signed grant field scan={kind: rerank, q, k}, applied by make_hpic_app's post-decryption filter hook); returns Top-k",
  "blas_threads": 1,
  "storage": "one SQLite file for all tenants, memory-mapped with a 256 MiB page cache (PRAGMA mmap_size=2147418112; PRAGMA cache_size=-262144), identical for both arms",
  "record": "field ref=item-<id>, keyword g<id//10>, vector, ~128 B UTF-8 memo text; the SDK also stores the raw vector inside the body",
  "oracle": "exhaustive FP64 cosine on the stored unit FP32 vectors, ties by id (0.9s, untimed)"
 },
